{
  "about": "Tile pixel rects as the Firmware draws them: ui_geometry.c and ui_tile_rect in ui_pages.c (firmware/components/td_ui_core). td_core::live::cell_rect, the app's geometry.ts and the Firmware host test (firmware/tools/test_tile_geometry.py) each reproduce every case. Coordinates are screen pixels; screen is already oriented, grid is the Page's rows/cols, and tile is its cell position and span. fullScreen uses the whole screen. Otherwise each design length is scaled by min(screen.w, screen.h)/600, truncating: title strip 56, pager strip 36, margin x 28, margin y 20, gap 16. The grid is the band between the strips, inset by the margins. Each cell edge is n * (grid_length + gap) / cells, truncating, and a Tile ends one gap before its far edge. An invalid grid (outside 1 to 8) or span gives the empty rect.",
